A reader's check of main's answers at Review 80 (agy-002's; row A15, not checked by main). The three planted
cases of the reader's finding are caught. Its fourth clause was not answered: no page, verdict line, ledger
or register row says that two later arcs raised the count of caught cases from 14 to 19 and to 24, and the
verdict line's own count is not held.

The page of B1890 and its verdict line each have a dated note after the sentence on the planted suite's
count: the suite has grown to 32 cases since; by that version main's head after this series caught 14; the
second series raised that to 19 (B1893) and the third to 24 (B1896). Each number is on the page of the arc
that ran it, and the lock reads it there: B1893's page for 14 and 19, B1896's for 19 and 24.

The lock also holds the verdict line's own count, the seat's 11 of 21, in the line and on the page.

No row of a ledger or of the register is written here: a row for it is for the series of registrations.

The lock passes: 9 tests. Every gate passes but the count of landings. Not checked by main.
